I’ll treat the concrete corner as the shared-tail model: top row `x` and corank rows `Y` multiply the same `2x2` tail `A`, so `B0=xA` and `Q_b=YA`. The answer depends on that sharing; collapsing `B0` to an independent coordinate would change the local model.
